{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040062-2e-guide-how-to-choose-your-obsessions","id":1040062,"title":"[2E] Guide - How to choose your Obsessions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T09:57:44-08:00","id":1040062,"title":"[2E] Guide - How to choose your Obsessions?","content":"Simple guide topic based on running Obsessions mechanics for 2 years in <b>Mage</b> games ( even prior to 2E corebook ).<br /> <br /> Main advise - <b>Try to phrase Obsessions <i>simpler</i></b>. My Guardian player had for a long time '<i>Are those Three Hieromagus?</i>' which give him Arcane Beats when he was checking over 3 PCs for signs for Messiah of Magic. BUT it <b>did not </b>let him take A-Beats for looking on general lore about Hieromagus in his or other Orders libraries or even looking in to messianic lore of Sleepers ( like Jesus, Budda and rest of them ). Simpler stated Obsession of '<i>Hieromagus</i>' works better here, as letting for more variety of scenes or even tempting players for A-Beats in varies situations - like examples mentioned before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>On general - stick to Mystery name as Obsession, maybe marking your theory as simple variant in </b><b>bracket</b><b>.</b> Many PCs and NPCs in my games have Obsessions of Time Before ( i.e. 'Atlantis' thing ) - I different them by giving in their main thought on it in bracket - so I have mages with '<i>Time Before ( Camelot )</i>', '<i>Time Before ( Metropolis )</i>', '<i>Time Before ( First Dream )</i>', etc. But each one of them will generally get A-Beat when seeing or looking for ANYTHING from Time Before - confronting this with their theory could just grant them <b><i>even more</i></b> A-Beats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the end, our Guardian player choose Obsessions of '<i>Hieromagus (Three?)</i>' marking both his dedication to general Mystery of Hieromagus and his own particular theory of other 3 players being candidates for title. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>As for examples or broadening your characters Obsessions options </b>- check <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991057-2e-orders-obsessions\">those I uncovered from Orders books and their dogmas</a>. They are great 'first Obsessions' for characters to start on.<br /> <br /> <b>Side Advise: </b>As ST, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895425-2e-hack-more-obsessions\">you can make a simple house rule and let players choose 1 extra Obsession</a> for general cabal / main plot Mystery - because starting with only 1 Obsessions is hard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:23:00-08:00","id":1040106,"title":"","content":"You don't really need more than one Obsession at the start. Assume a Mage starts with no Obsessions except the plot relevant one, and they gain more as they get to know what their character is actually interested in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:27:20-08:00","id":1040111,"title":"","content":"Eh, that depends. A lot of characters *is* definied by their Obsession, and often, this Obsession isn't immediately plot-related. I can see a situation where your Obsession isn't pinged for numerous sessions simply because it doesn't align with the current plot. For situations like those, extra slot can be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:43:53-08:00","id":1040185,"title":"","content":"Typically, I find it's the other way around, what the character is like defines what their Obsession will be. Which is why I'm fine with recommending that they take a story related Obsession first and branch out into more personal Obsessions later on as the players become accustomed to their characters. That's just a matter of preference though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:39:11-08:00","id":1040217,"title":"","content":"It probably is. I tend to make character before the game and create a fairly complete picture of them, so they usually have something going on for them before the plot is introduced. Other players I've seen like to base their character around a Obsession to create a theme or get inspired, too. So for people like that, the extra slot might be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T19:47:17-08:00","id":1041061,"title":"","content":"Latest iteration of Order's Obsessions, for ease of use with previous advises. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sum up: <b>Characters can take more broad interpretations of their Orders Mysteries as his more broader Obsession, in contrast to other mages, more limited in those categories.</b><br /> <br /> * <b>Adamantine Arrows</b> - <i>Oaths</i> - Examples are classical 'Protect my cabal'<br /> * <b>Free Council</b> - <i>Techne</i> - Examples are various Sleepers occult traditions or technical disciplines Also, parts of Libertine Creed - one players choose for our game 'Servants of Lie' as his Obsession. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> * <b>Guardians of Veil </b>- <i>Persons and Beings</i> - Abyssal Intruders and Hieromagus are examples, particular Sleeper in Labyrinth would be other.<br /> * <b>Mysterium</b> - <i>Disciplines of Order</i> - I.E.<ul><li>Magosophy</li> <li>Supernology</li> <li>Thaumatology</li> <li>Occultism</li> <li>Sidereology</li> <li>Teratology</li> <li>Exoterics ( Each one of Sleepers arts and humanities )</li> </ul>* <b>Silver Ladder </b>- <i>Persons and Institutions</i> - Elemental Pilgrimage and Lion-Sage-Stag are particulars in here, promising Sleeper student would be other. Looking over church, company or government office.<br /> * <b>Seers of Throne</b> - Signs of Exarchs - Mystery Commands are particulars here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}